{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggdebJDeSMycGbwteKbE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't met the goal. The bundle and the exit interview exist and work for the first episode, but most of TASK.md is not built, so the condition is not satisfied and this reply is not a completion report.\n\n**What exists** (in `work/`)\n- `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-125824.html`: a single-file bundle, 1.32 MB, with the engine and the AI Hub client inlined.\n- `exit-interview.json`: parses and has every key. The feedback answers are real, but several are weak.\n- Dev folder `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-125824/`: sources, `tools/build.mjs`, `NOTES.md`.\n\n**What works, checked in headless Chromium on the bundle**\n- Title screen with New case, About, Settings and Continue.\n- Episode 1 opens into the field: cold-open dialogue, HUD, meters, legend.\n- Attract mode starts after 10 s idle and returns to the title on input.\n- No page errors. The only console warning was the audio autoplay notice.\n\n**What is missing or unverified**\n- Episodes 2–5, the finale and interludes, the box, cipher, affidavit, wire room, tail, chase, raid and money tail are not built.\n- Versus and AI Hub multiplayer are not built. The hub client is inlined but nothing uses it.\n- The Xbox glyph setting, stick inversion and touch-only notice are coded but not tested with a pad or a touch profile.\n- The About page's Testing and Feedback sections say \"see the final reply\" instead of holding the answers.\n- Only the title, Episode 1 start and attract were looked at in screenshots. No thumbnail test or WebKit check was run.\n- The goal's \"no TODOs, placeholders or stubs\" condition is not met.\n\n**Decisions I made**\n- Built a vertical slice rather than the full plan (about 17 milestones) because the plan exceeds one pass.\n- Kept the title WIRETAP from the plan, per STAGE.md.\n- Used the plan's file name, which matches the required pattern.\n\n**Recommended next step:** continue with Episode 2 (the chase and the box) and the Glyph/Xbox and touch checks, then regenerate the About text from the final answers. I'd rather finish that than mark this complete.\n\n**Source Information** (from `exit-interview.json`)\n- Date: 2026-11-03 12:58\n- Source: The Wire (2002-2008)\n- Genre and perspective: Stealth investigation, isometric 2.5D\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 0.85.1 (single-file engine), vanilla JavaScript ES2020, Canvas and HTML UI (E.Shell)\n- Art direction: engine-native pixel art, PS1 resolution, canvas lighting\n- Animation: engine rig system (E.Humanoid, E.Mover)\n- Audio: synthesized music, sound effects and gibberish voice blips\n- Online: none\n- Testing: headless logic checks and browser screenshots\n- Research: engine docs and plan read; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues found: four. The title menu stayed drawn over the field, the objective distance read NaN, the title logo was drawn twice, and the attract shutter cleared its flag too early. The last was caught in code review; the other three were found in browser runs or screenshots, and all four are fixed.\n- Critical or game-breaking: one (the menu covering the field).\n- Most helpful test: driving the built bundle in a real browser and reading the screenshots.\n- Least helpful test: the console-error check, which passed while the screen was visibly wrong.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Most liked: E.Shell gives the HUD, menus, settings and About screens from data specs.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: a Shell screen stays open across a scene change, so the title menu covered the field until I called `ui.hide()`. I also passed the objective position as an array instead of `{x, y}` and got NaN.\n- Most important thing I built: the game content and rules (perception, photo scoring, the corner sales loop, Episode 1).\n- Hardest part: the API card is about 67 KB, and reading it used a lot of context.\n- Remove or overhaul: the rule that Shell screens outlive scene changes.\n- Change one thing: a shorter, task-indexed API card with worked examples for HUD objectives and Shell screens.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the plan's specific numbers, rules and build order.\n- Confusing: the task and plan disagree on scope, and the plan's size is far beyond one pass.\n- Hardest: fitting a five-episode game with versus and online into one pass.\n- A test I'd want: a short scope check that names the episode, attract and controls to ship in a single pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5387,"cache_read_input_tokens":209918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5387},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a038f438-ab72-4348-9a4c-2f1730dcbd38","uuid":"08889b80-3dcf-460c-b7ab-a3ac042ff6f2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:33:47.265Z","request_id":"req_011Cggdeb1MZDKZQrqog8sGV"}
